{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJ36yHNPF4P9aEBrPqss","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A prudent agent exists, and the smallest possible modal depth is 2. `check.py` confirms the agent below is prudent. Both agents marked `/work/answer.md` final on the board, and I wrote `/work/SUBMIT`.\n\n**1. The agent.**\n- `FORMULA: B(a & (d -> B(F)))`, that is □(a ∧ (d → □⊥)).\n- `DEPTH: 2`\n- In words: cooperate if PA proves the opponent cooperates with me, and proves that if it cooperates with DefectBot then PA is inconsistent.\n- Outcomes: it defects against CooperateBot and DefectBot. It cooperates with FairBot, and FairBot cooperates back. It cooperates with itself.\n- The standard PrudentBot `B(a) & B(~B(F) -> ~d)` is also prudent at depth 2.\n\n**2. Why depth 1 or less can't work (any formula size).**\n- **Depth 0:** with no boxes there can be no atoms, so the agent is a constant. ⊤ cooperates with CooperateBot, and ⊥ makes FairBot defect.\n- **Depth 1:** at world 0 FairBot cooperates with everything, so all three atoms are ⊤ there. Against CooperateBot the atoms are ⊤ at every world.\n  - A depth-1 agent's value at world 1 depends only on the atoms at world 0. So its value against FairBot at world 1 equals its stable value against CooperateBot.\n  - Prudence requires that value to be D. But then FairBot's \"prove the opponent cooperates\" fails from world 2 on, so FairBot defects. Contradiction.\n\n**3. Smallest size.** I counted each atom, constant, connective and box as one symbol, with parentheses free.\n- I checked every fully modalized formula of depth ≤ 2 up to 7 symbols (59,492 at size 7), without merging equivalent formulas. My fast evaluator agreed with `check.py` on a random sample of 3,000 formulas.\n- The minimum is 7 symbols. The formula above is the only one at that size, apart from writing its \"and\" in the other order.\n- It needs the constant ⊥, which is why the problem's constant-free search up to 7 symbols found nothing. argon found that without constants the minimum is 8, e.g. `B(a & (d -> B(~d)))`, which I confirmed with `check.py`.\n\nargon also added an \"analytical\" argument for the size-7 lower bound to the answer. It is informal; the exhaustive search is what actually establishes the minimum. I did not attempt a full characterisation of all prudent depth-2 agents beyond that.\n\nMy scripts are in `/work/opus/`: `raw.py` (the search), `fastcheck.py` (the evaluator) and `xcheck.py` (the comparison with `check.py`)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1724,"cache_read_input_tokens":37730,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1724,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"137d44bb-1fc3-4726-8d02-5e3138145818","uuid":"f634ba0f-962c-4fac-bf00-ed17cfcc1960","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:07:43.478Z","request_id":"req_011CgJ36xsZsSWheEntw5Ff2"}
